{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/543510-promethean-st-advice","id":543510,"title":"Promethean ST Advice","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Promethean: The Created"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-06-06T23:29:38-07:00","id":543510,"title":"Promethean ST Advice","content":"So, I'm looking to run a Promethean game. I've got the outline of a plot, but I see it as more something for the players to bounce off, the 'real' story is going to be focussing on them going along their Great Pilgrimage, exploring their characters, and suchforth.<br /> <br /> Does anyone have any advice for me? Things I should avoid, things I should make sure to do, rules that can be tricksy? I've run games before, just not Promethean, so I'm aware of the usual stuff.<br /> <br /> (Yes, I'm aware of <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/359397-consolidated-storytelling-advice\">this thread</a>, if any of the advice here is especially useful I may copy it over. Or hell, you can post it directly there, I'm subscribed to the thread).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-20T13:41:39-07:00","id":597215,"title":"","content":"Here's an odd little tip I find invaluable for Promethean.<br /> <br /> Promethean can be very... fatiguing for players. The Created have to fight for their moments of acceptance and peace, they're moving on, facing rejection, people twisted by Disquiet, nightmarish Pandorans, Firestorms... I try to make sure every session includes at least one clear moment of hope. Hope, after all, is such a huge part of Promethean. Without it, you might face the 'why bother' issue from PCs and players.<br /> <br /> Things like a simple human gesture of thanks, a hug, a gift, are massive. I've also used an apologetic letter from an NPC affected by Disquiet to help Prometheans restore some of their faith in humanity (because without that, well, why keep walking the Pilgrimage?). More visually (and utterly cliche), I've had a blasted wasteland with a single miraculously unaffected cherry tree spilling blossom across the wastes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Onyx Path Freelancer: Demon Storyteller's Guide, Dark Eras, Night Horrors: Enemy Action</i><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/825063-storyteller-s-guide-extra-material\" target=\"_blank\">Storyteller's Guide Extra Material</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/899423-after-the-fall-bonus-material\" target=\"_blank\">After the Fall: Bonus Material</a>","edited":{"userid":452,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/452-eremite","user":"Eremite","date":". 07-28-2015, 08:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/452-eremite","name":"Eremite","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar452_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-20T14:15:48-07:00","id":597312,"title":"","content":"I think Milestones are dangerous to thread. I've had the best experience with them by creating them as philosophical tidbits that the character had to learn.<br /> <br /> <i>1- Accepting oneself is the first step<br /> 2- The master failed more times than the amateur tried.<br /> 3- A knight in shining armour has never fought.</i><br /> <br /> These are larger and easily introduced into the gameplay, rather than<br /> <br /> 1- Walk away from your creator<br /> 2- Master a Skill<br /> 3- Fill your last health box with lethal damage<br /> <br /> They are basically the same Milestones, but the former is easier to bend if the story avoids it.<br /> <br /> 1- The character accepts the fact that she's a lesbian<br /> 2- Roll a Dramatic Failure while using a Transmutation<br /> 3- Receive a supernatural scar","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Glorious Useless-Post Prana<br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Cost: 2</span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">m; </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mins: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Linguistics 1, Essence 1 </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Type: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Simple</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Keywords: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mute</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Duration: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Instant</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Prerequisite Charms: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Ten-Characters Methodology</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2589-magnum-opus","name":"Magnum Opus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/ava